<!--
  Scenario catalog strings, Santali (Ol Chiki).

  Sentences are kept short and imperative on purpose. This is the language most likely to be read by someone
  who reads slowly, and a long clause is a clause that gets skipped — which in a timed safety drill shows up as
  hesitation the worker did not actually have.

  Industrial terms with no settled Santali equivalent are transliterated rather than invented: ᱢᱮᱥᱤᱱ, ᱦᱟᱨᱱᱮᱥ,
  ᱯᱚᱨᱢᱤᱴ, ᱠᱚᱱᱵᱷᱮᱭᱚᱨ. That is what Santali-medium safety material does, and a coined word nobody recognises is
  worse than a borrowed one everybody does.

  Needs review by a native Santali speaker familiar with mine-site vocabulary before a field pilot. Coverage is
  complete; wording quality is a separate question and pretending otherwise would be dishonest.
-->
